 go over the 168-unit warehouse limit, so a few units are lost. The loss is only their purchase price, which is small.\n- **Plan 2:** product 0 at forecast loses about 260 in shortfalls compared with 1.2×.\n- **Plan 6:** product 1 at 1.05× loses about 500 compared with 1.2×.\n- **Plan 7:** it is about 1.1× on a two-day cycle, much like plan 3.\n- **Plan 4:** it orders every day, which costs about 728 more in fixed order fees than ordering every other day. It saves only about 430 in storage.\n- **Plan 5:** it orders every third day at forecast level. It runs short (for example, it orders 95 of product 0 for a 111-unit stretch) and goes over capacity more often.\n- **Cash:** no plan runs out of money.\n\n**Robustness.** The plans that order more are more stable when demand comes in high, which is where the costly shortfalls are. Going over capacity mostly hits product 1, but that only wastes cheap purchase cost.\n\n**Ranking:** 0 and 3 first, then 2 and 7, then 6, 4, 1, 5."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 4932, "cache_read_input_tokens": 886, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 4932}, "output_tokens": 3, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-29T07:40:27.391Z", "request_id": "req_011CgW9aCAXBQKDeXRRFPKVd"}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_stop", "index": 1}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_start", "index": 2, "content_block": {"type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01DYc6vHYUoksjmRes2eBBfU", "name": "StructuredOutput", "input": {}, "caller": {"type": "direct"}}}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011CgW9aCP